Method Request → Response Least role Notes RunAudit RunAuditRequest → stream AuditProgress editor RunAudit starts (or attaches to, or resumes) the caller’s audit of a domain and streams stage progress until the run ends. A second call for the same (caller, domain) while a run is active attaches to it; a call after a failed/partial run resumes from the first stage that is not done; a call within 24h of a completed run returns that run unless force is set. A score_only call is its own run: it never attaches to or replays a full audit (nor a full audit to it); see RunAuditRequest.score_only. GetAuditRun GetAuditRunRequest → AuditRun viewer ListAuditRuns ListAuditRunsRequest → ListAuditRunsResponse viewer GetAuditAiVisibility GetAuditAiVisibilityRequest → AuditAiVisibility viewer GetAuditAiVisibility returns what a run’s genai_visibility stage measured, finding by finding, with the evidence for each. GetAuditFindings GetAuditFindingsRequest → AuditFindings viewer GetAuditFindings returns what a run found for the business: leads with their contacts, possible competitors, where it wins and loses against each, niches worth exploring and partners with their contacts. Each kind says whether it was found, found nothing, or was not measured. DeleteAuditRuns DeleteAuditRunsRequest → DeleteAuditRunsResponse editor DeleteAuditRuns deletes some of the caller’s full audit runs, or every run of one domain but the newest (all_but_latest, with the domain typed back as confirm). Removed: each run, its stages, its findings, its AI-visibility rows and its content-gaps snapshot unless a campaign plan uses it. Kept: leads, campaigns, drafts, the diagnosis and the site-score history. A run still in flight is refused, never deleted. GetAuditAudience GetAuditAudienceRequest → AuditAudience viewer GetAuditAudience returns who a run found the business sells to and what it sells (the research inputs it saved), each with where it came from. Also uses AuditAction.
// AuditReport is the full audit result: the output contract of the scoring // engine. overall_score is the weighted mean of composites; benchmark_mode is // "relative" or "absolute"; skipped_data_sources lists adapters the user could // configure to raise coverage. message AuditReport { string url = 1; google.protobuf.Timestamp audited_at = 2; double overall_score = 3; repeated AuditComposite composites = 4; repeated string skipped_data_sources = 5; string benchmark_mode = 6; repeated AuditRecommendation recommendations = 7; repeated AuditAction actions = 8; } // AuditComposite is one of the four scored dimensions. coverage is the fraction // (0-1) of the composite's weight that was actually scored — a 90 at 0.4 // coverage is very different from a 90 at 1.0. message AuditComposite { string id = 1; string label = 2; double score = 3; double weight = 4; // normalized 0-1 double coverage = 5; // 0-1 repeated AuditSignal signals = 6; } // AuditSignal is a scored signal within a composite. message AuditSignal { string id = 1; double score = 2; double weight = 3; // normalized 0-1 within its composite double coverage = 4; // 0-1 repeated AuditCheck checks = 5; } // AuditCheck is a single check's outcome. status is "scored" | "skipped" | // "error"; mode is "relative" | "absolute" for benchmark checks (else empty). message AuditCheck { string id = 1; double score = 2; string status = 3; string raw_value = 4; string notes = 5; string mode = 6; } // AuditRecommendation is a lowest-scoring check surfaced by global weighted // impact (check_weight × signal_weight × composite_weight), so the biggest // wins bubble up. message AuditRecommendation { string check_id = 1; double score = 2; double impact = 3; string notes = 4; } message RunAuditRequest { string domain = 1; // "example.com", "https://example.com/…" — normalised server-side bool force = 2; // start a fresh run even when a completed one is < 24h old // What the person told the audit about the business. Any field set starts a // fresh run built on it; a niche, industry or business name lets the // research stages start without waiting for the model to infer one. AuditTuning tuning = 3; // score_only runs only normalize + score, on the URL exactly as given, as a // tracked run of its own (not listed by ListAuditRuns). It attaches only to // an identical score_only run in flight and is never replayed from a stored // run. A score computed by an earlier score_only call with the same inputs // within PULSE_AUDIT_CACHE_TTL is reused unless force is set. bool score_only = 4; // Weighting profile (e.g. "ai-focused"), empty = default. score_only only. string scoring_profile = 5; // 2-3 competitor URLs switch the benchmark-dependent checks to relative // mode. score_only only. repeated string competitor_urls = 6; } // The new-audit form's details. Every field is optional. message AuditTuning { string business_name = 1; string industry = 2; string niche = 3; string target_audience = 4; string competitors = 5; // free text: names or URLs, comma separated string business_description = 6; // "What do you sell?" plus any extra context repeated string goals = 7; string linkedin_url = 8; string instagram_handle = 9; // Material uploaded through AuditAttachmentService (photos, a short video, // product documents, voice notes) the audit compares the brand against. // Owner scoped: an id that is not the caller's is refused. repeated string attachment_ids = 10; // "Where are most of your customers?" — asked only when the site did not // state it; used as the region only when no check on the site measures one. string customer_region = 11; } // AuditProvenance says where a stage's output came from: "sourced" (read from // the web), "inferred" (the model's reasoning over sourced input), or "mixed". message AuditProvenance { string kind = 1; // sourced | inferred | mixed | none repeated string source_urls = 2; // bounded; the pages the stage actually read string basis = 3; // one line: what the inference rests on } // AuditProgress is one event of a run. A stage event has stage set; the run's // terminal event has stage == "" and run_status set to its final value. message AuditProgress { string run_id = 1; string stage = 2; // normalize, crawl, score, trends, diagnosis, fanout_*, niche, radar_*, leads string status = 3; // pending | running | done | failed | skipped string detail = 4; map<string, int32> counts = 5; string error = 6; // set whenever status is failed (and on a failed/partial terminal event) AuditProvenance provenance_summary = 7; int32 queue_position = 8; // >0 while this stage waits for the model lane string run_status = 9; // running | completed | partial | failed string domain = 10; string diagnostic_id = 11; bool attached = 12; // this stream joined a run another call started int32 attempt = 13; } message AuditStage { string stage = 1; string status = 2; int32 attempt = 3; map<string, int32> counts = 4; string error = 5; string detail = 6; google.protobuf.Timestamp started_at = 7; google.protobuf.Timestamp finished_at = 8; } message AuditRun { string id = 1; string domain = 2; string diagnostic_id = 3; string status = 4; // running | completed | partial | failed google.protobuf.Timestamp created_at = 5; google.protobuf.Timestamp finished_at = 6; repeated AuditStage stages = 7; // The site score the run's score stage saved; unset when it saved none. AuditReport score_report = 8; bool score_only = 9; } message GetAuditRunRequest { string run_id = 1; } message ListAuditRunsRequest { int32 limit = 1; // default 20, max 100 string domain = 2; // optional filter } message ListAuditRunsResponse { repeated AuditRun runs = 1; } message GetAuditAiVisibilityRequest { string run_id = 1; } // One AI-access requirement read from the site itself. message AiAccessCheck { string kind = 1; // crawler | llms_txt | server_rendered | structured_data string item = 2; // the crawler's name, or the file / page checked string state = 3; // pass | fail | not_measured string evidence = 4; // the line that decided it string evidence_url = 5; // The site-score check whose fix-artifact (in the score report's actions, // applied through ApplyAuditActions) fixes a failure; "" when none does. string fix_check_id = 6; } // One buyer question read on a search engine's own result page. message AiAnswerCheck { string question = 1; string basis = 2; // what the question was derived from string engine = 3; // the engine whose page was read string serp_url = 4; // that page // cited | not_cited | no_ai_answer | not_measured. not_measured is never // counted as not cited. string state = 5; string why = 6; // set when not_measured repeated string sources = 7; // the AI answer's cited links repeated string competitors_cited = 8; // cited hosts matching a named competitor repeated string other_cited = 9; // every other cited host int32 organic_rank = 10; // the brand's position among organic results; 0 = not among them int32 organic_count = 11; // organic results on the page as loaded; 0 = page not read } message AuditAiVisibility { string run_id = 1; string domain = 2; bool measured = 3; // false: the stage stored nothing (absent, not empty) repeated AiAccessCheck access = 4; repeated AiAnswerCheck answers = 5; string engines_covered = 6; // e.g. "DuckDuckGo" string not_covered = 7; // what this measurement does not read } message GetAuditFindingsRequest { string run_id = 1; // "" = the caller's latest full audit } // FindingContact is what a page publishes about how to reach someone. message FindingContact { string email = 1; string phone = 2; string website = 3; string linkedin = 4; } message AuditFinding { string kind = 1; // lead | competitor | advantage | niche | partner string title = 2; // the company, competitor, niche or partner string detail = 3; // why, in plain words string source_url = 4; // where it was found or measured string basis = 5; // measured | named (by the owner) | judged (model proposal the plan gate kept) FindingContact contact = 6; repeated string wins = 7; // advantage: checks this business meets and the competitor does not repeated string losses = 8; // advantage: checks the competitor meets and this business does not string lead_id = 9; // lead: its row on the Leads page string judgement = 10; // judged: the plan gate's verdict bool measured = 11; // false = this item could not be measured (detail says why) string id = 12; // the finding's own id (a partner's automation target id) } // AuditFindingKind is one kind's state for the run. message AuditFindingKind { string kind = 1; string state = 2; // found | none_found | not_measured string why = 3; // none_found / not_measured: the stage's own reason string stage = 4; // the stage that produced it } message AuditFindings { string run_id = 1; string domain = 2; repeated AuditFinding findings = 3; repeated AuditFindingKind kinds = 4; } message DeleteAuditRunsRequest { repeated string run_ids = 1; // the caller's runs to delete // Delete every run of domain except its newest; confirm must equal the // domain as ListAuditRuns returns it (the typed confirmation). bool all_but_latest = 2; string domain = 3; string confirm = 4; // With all_but_latest: delete the newest run too. bool include_latest = 5; // START OVER (Settings › Account, Brand Analysis history): every run of the // caller (this account or agency client only) AND what the runs produced — // stages, findings, AI-visibility rows, site scores, insight snapshots // (content gaps, scenarios), every diagnosis, follow-up cycles with their // tasks and check-ins, market research (summaries, channels, trending posts, // imported partners), campaign proposals never accepted with their // campaigns, drafts never approved with their scheduled rows, creative // briefs and course outlines the audits made, and the leads they found. // confirm must equal domain, a domain the caller audited. Refused while any // of the caller's audits is running. Never deleted: anything published, // measured results (post_results), integrations, leads added by hand, // imported or won. bool start_over = 6; // Start over also deletes accepted campaigns (with their plans and roadmap). bool also_accepted_campaigns = 7; // No longer read: start over always deletes the leads audits found // (source "scraped" or linked from a finding) unless won (owner, 2026-10-30). bool also_audit_leads = 8; // Start over also deletes approved or scheduled items not sent yet. bool also_approved_unsent = 9; // Count what would go, delete nothing (the dialog's preview). bool dry_run = 10; } // What DeleteAuditRuns removed, row by row. message DeleteAuditRunsResponse { repeated string deleted_run_ids = 1; int32 stages = 2; int32 findings = 3; int32 ai_visibility = 4; int32 snapshots = 5; // Runs still in flight: never deleted. repeated string refused_run_ids = 6; // Start over only (0 for a plain delete). int32 campaign_plans = 7; int32 campaigns = 8; int32 drafts = 9; // content rows never approved int32 approved_unsent = 10; // approved or scheduled, not sent (only when asked) int32 scheduled_posts = 11; // pending scheduled posts removed with them int32 leads = 12; // only when asked int32 roadmap_items = 13; int32 planner_tasks = 14; int32 diagnostics = 15; int32 competitor_channels = 16; // Published items kept (never deleted), for the dialog's summary. int32 kept_published = 17; bool dry_run = 18; // Start over refused: an audit is running (its run id). string refused_running = 19; int32 trending_posts = 20; // trending posts the research saved for the runs' niches // Start over (owner, 2026-10-30: "clear everything the audits produced"). int32 cycles = 21; // follow-up cycles the audits made, with their tasks int32 check_ins = 22; // the weekly check-ins of those cycles int32 creatives = 23; // creative briefs the audits made int32 courses = 24; // course outlines the audits made int32 market_summaries = 25; // radar summaries int32 partners = 26; // partners imported from the research (hand-added ones stay) int32 site_scores = 27; // site scores the runs saved // What stays, for the dialog: leads added by hand, imported or won; // accepted campaigns (only when the person keeps them); connected accounts. int32 kept_leads = 28; int32 kept_campaigns = 29; int32 kept_integrations = 30; } message GetAuditAudienceRequest { string run_id = 1; } // One group of people the business sells to, as the run found them. message AudiencePersona { string name = 1; string source = 2; // tuning | owner | leads | audience string evidence = 3; // the line it was drawn from ("" when none was kept) } // One thing the business sells, in the site's own words when read there. message AudienceOffering { string name = 1; string quote = 2; // the site's words ("" when the owner typed it) string source = 3; // site | tuning string source_url = 4; // the page read ("" for the owner's own words) } message AuditAudience { string run_id = 1; string domain = 2; // false: the run saved no audience (absent, not empty). bool measured = 3; repeated AudiencePersona personas = 4; repeated AudienceOffering offerings = 5; repeated string problems = 6; // the problems the research found for them }

data.contentresearchservice#ContentResearchSe:
ContentResearchService — the audit’s deep content research (release 5). From what an audit MEASURED (the site’s own text and what it sells, the niche, trending posts, competitor channels, trend searches, leads and the people the business sells to), PULSE fans out scenarios: one person × one problem they have × one angle × the channel formats it suits, each with 3-5 post ideas, the findings that back it and a research pass through PULSE’s own crawler. Every scenario is one content-skill run on PULSE’s own inference (OpenBias, Go checks, plan gate); a withheld one is listed with the reason. Nothing here publishes.
